 ENVIRONMENT / PROVENANCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  .NET SDK 10.0.300 present; TeslaSync.App.Core builds clean (pure C#).
  The generated prompt's literal output paths (apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/
  Sharing/*.xaml) do NOT match this repo. The real app is the C#-MARKUP project
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App (feature views are *.cs UserControls, NOT XAML), with
  the testable UI-free logic split into *.Model/.Source/.ViewModel.cs that
  TeslaSync.App.Tests <Compile Include>s and verifies headlessly. To avoid silent
  drift (covenant #9) the page was implemented in the REAL project conventions
  (mirroring feature-views/DriveDetailPage), not as an orphan XAML file that would
  never compile.

  ROOT-CAUSE (pre-existing, committed at HEAD, git status clean):
  Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs had an UNCLOSED lambda in the "Locations" page-factory
  registration (missing `return page; });`). This CS syntax error (CS1002/CS1026/
  CS1513) failed CoreCompile, which CASCADED into 84 WinUI XAML-compiler errors
  (WMC0001 "unknown type" + WMC9999 NRE) that masked the true cause. The whole
  TeslaSync.App never built. Fixed minimally in the same constructor I had to edit
  to register SharedDrive (allowed file: "NavigationView registration"; covenant —
  a tightly-coupled bug in code being changed). After the fix the full solution
  builds with 0 errors and 0 WMC errors — the environment builds WinUI fine.

